  {
    "description": "Poll the status of a background command launched by sonarr_run_command or sonarr_import_folder, or the moveCommandId returned by sonarr_update_series and sonarr_bulk_edit_series.",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "commandId": {
          "description": "Command id",
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "minimum": -9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "commandId",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_get_command",
  },
  {
    "description": "List available quality profiles. Use these ids in sonarr_add_series and sonarr_update_series.",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_list_quality_profiles",
  },
  {
    "description": "List configured root folders where series are stored (id, path, accessible, free space, unmapped folder count). Use these paths in sonarr_add_series; use sonarr_list_unmapped_folders for the folders themselves.",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_list_root_folders",
  },
  {
    "description": "List all tags available for series organization.",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_list_tags",
  },
  {
    "description": "Get Sonarr status in one call: system (version, branch, OS, Docker, start time), health (the health check warnings and errors about the installation) and disks (free and total bytes on each drive containing series or root folders).",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_get_status",
  },
  {
    "description": "Run a live interactive search across indexers for episode or season releases (can take several seconds). Results are in Sonarr's preference order with rank. Rejections are Sonarr's verbatim reasons for not choosing a release automatically. Use guid + indexerId with sonarr_grab_release.",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "approvedOnly": {
          "description": "Show only Sonarr-approved releases (default false)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "episodeId": {
          "description": "Episode id for single-episode search",
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "minimum": -9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Maximum results to return (default 20)",
          "maximum": 100,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "seasonNumber": {
          "description": "Season number for season-pack search",
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "minimum": -9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "seriesId": {
          "description": "Series id for season-pack search",
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "minimum": -9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "titleContains": {
          "description": "Case-insensitive substring filter (e.g. "MeGusta")",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_search_releases",
  },
  {
    "description": "Download a release via Sonarr. Grab uses cached search results (expire ~30 minutes); if grab fails, run sonarr_search_releases again. Grab overrides Sonarr's decision to DOWNLOAD but rejections can still block IMPORT, leaving items stuck in queue. Starts a real download tracked and imported by Sonarr (unlike prowlarr_grab_release, which bypasses Sonarr).",
    "effect": "destructive",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "guid": {
          "description": "Release guid from sonarr_search_releases",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "indexerId": {
          "description": "Release indexerId from sonarr_search_releases",
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "minimum": -9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "guid",
        "indexerId",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_grab_release",
  },
  {
    "description": "Bulk edit multiple series at once. Only fields explicitly provided are updated; omitted fields are not changed. Supports changing root folder, quality profile, series type, monitored state, season folder setting, and tags. When rootFolderPath is given, moveFiles is required: true moves the files with the records, false repoints the records only (the files stay put and Sonarr reports the episodes missing after a rescan). With moveFiles true, Sonarr queues the move as a background command and returns before the files move: the result carries moveCommandId to poll with sonarr_get_command (null when none was found). At most 10 ids are accepted per call when moveFiles is true; send larger sets as sequential batches, and poll each moveCommandId until it completes before the next batch or a retry.",
    "effect": "destructive",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "applyTags": {
          "description": "How to apply tags (default replace)",
          "enum": [
            "add",
            "remove",
            "replace",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "monitored": {
          "description": "Set monitored state",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "moveFiles": {
          "description": "Required with rootFolderPath: true moves the files, false repoints the records only",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "qualityProfileId": {
          "description": "From sonarr_list_quality_profiles",
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "minimum": -9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "rootFolderPath": {
          "description": "Root folder path from sonarr_list_root_folders",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "seasonFolder": {
          "description": "Use season folders",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "seriesIds": {
          "description": "Series ids to update",
          "items": {
            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
            "minimum": -9007199254740991,
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "type": "array",
        },
        "seriesType": {
          "description": "Series type",
          "enum": [
            "standard",
            "daily",
            "anime",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "tags": {
          "description": "Tag ids from sonarr_list_tags",
          "items": {
            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
            "minimum": -9007199254740991,
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "type": "array",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "seriesIds",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_bulk_edit_series",
  },
  {
    "description": "List folders in each root folder that are not yet mapped to any series. Use this to find media that needs to be imported or organized.",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_list_unmapped_folders",
  },
  {
    "description": "Preview how Sonarr will rename episode files for a series or season without actually running the rename. Useful for verifying your naming rules are working correctly. At most 100 previews are returned; \`total\` gives the full count.",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "seasonNumber": {
          "description": "Season number (all seasons if omitted)",
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "minimum": -9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "seriesId": {
          "description": "Sonarr series id",
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "minimum": -9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "seriesId",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_get_rename_preview",
  },
  {
    "description": "Find potential duplicate series in the library. Detects series with the same tvdbId (exact duplicate) and different series (distinct tvdbIds) with the same normalized title + year under different root folders (likely misplaced copies). Helps identify library organization issues. Results may be up to 30 s old (writes made through this server show up at once); pass refresh: true for a fresh read.",
    "effect": "read",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "refresh": {
          "description": "Download the library again instead of reusing a copy up to 30 s old (default false)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_find_duplicate_series",
  },
  {
    "description": "Scan a folder and import any episode files found into existing series entries in Sonarr. This is asynchronous — it returns a command id that can be polled with sonarr_get_command. Important: the series must already exist in Sonarr for files to attach to it; otherwise the scan will not import them. Use folderPath from sonarr_list_unmapped_folders.",
    "effect": "destructive",
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "importMode": {
          "description": "How to handle files: Auto (default, let Sonarr decide), Move (relocate to configured library), Copy (keep original, duplicate to library)",
          "enum": [
            "Auto",
            "Move",
            "Copy",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "path": {
          "description": "Absolute path to the folder to import, as returned by sonarr_list_unmapped_folders (folderPath field)",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "path",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "sonarr_import_folder",
  },
]
`;
